“The 

**********Extracted claims**********

Senator Peter Welch, a Democrat from Vermont, became the first Democratic senator to call on President Joe Biden to step aside as the party’s presidential nominee.
Senator Welch's call was published in a Washington Post op-ed.
Senator Welch expressed great respect for President Joe Biden in his op-ed.
Senator Welch stated that President Joe Biden's debate performance was disastrous.
Senator Welch stated that President Joe Biden needs to reassess whether he is the best candidate for the presidency.
Senator Welch expressed his view that President Joe Biden is not the best candidate.
Senator Welch called on President Joe Biden to withdraw from the race for the good of the country.
Senator Welch described Vice President Kamala Harris as a capable and proven leader.
Senator Welch stated that the Democratic party has other electable, young, and energizing Democratic governors and senators in swing states.
Senator Welch's comments make him the 10th congressional Democrat to call on President Joe Biden to step aside.
The other nine congressional Democrats who called on President Joe Biden to step aside were former colleagues of Senator Welch in the House.
Senator Michael Bennet, a Democrat from Colorado, became the first Democratic senator to publicly state he does not believe President Joe Biden is capable of winning reelection.
Senator Michael Bennet did not call for President Joe Biden to withdraw.
Senator Michael Bennet stated that Donald Trump is on track to win the election.
Senator Michael Bennet stated that Donald Trump might win the election by a landslide.
