Russia was not invited to the previous peace conference held in Switzerland last month.
Volodymyr Zelensky previously stated that any talks with Russia could only happen after a Russian withdrawal from Ukraine.
Kyiv is facing a difficult frontline situation.
Kyiv is facing political uncertainty regarding the level of future support from Ukraine’s allies.
The progress of Russian troops in eastern Ukraine has slowed significantly since US weapons began arriving in May.
The progress of Russian troops in eastern Ukraine has not stopped entirely.
Russia is still gaining territory in Ukraine.
Russia is gaining territory at a slower pace.
Questions exist regarding the willingness of some of Ukraine's allies, including the United States and Germany, to continue providing resources for the conflict.
Volodymyr Zelensky stated that Ukraine is not receiving enough Western assistance to win the war.
Volodymyr Zelensky stated that the outcome of the war will be determined beyond Ukraine’s borders.
Volodymyr Zelensky stated that the war's outcome depends on finance, weapons, political support, and unity in the EU, NATO, and the world.
