Donald Trump stated he would "bring peace to the world and end the war that has cost so many lives."
Volodymyr Zelensky stated that he and Donald Trump discussed steps to make peace fair and lasting.
Russian President Vladimir Putin has stated multiple times that he is willing to negotiate with Ukraine.
Vladimir Putin's proposed terms for negotiation are unacceptable to Ukraine and its Western allies.
Vladimir Putin stated that Russia would end its war in Ukraine if Kyiv surrendered the entirety of four regions: Donetsk, Luhansk, Kherson, and Zaporizhzhia.
Moscow claims these four regions.
Large parts of Donetsk, Luhansk, Kherson, and Zaporizhzhia remain under Ukrainian control.
