Orysia Lutsevych stated that Ukraine is willing to sit at the negotiating table.
Orysia Lutsevych stated that any negotiations cannot be entirely on Russian terms.
Orysia Lutsevych stated that negotiations cannot lead to Ukraine's capitulation to Russia.
Orysia Lutsevych stated that Vladimir Putin is demanding control of regions he cannot conquer militarily.
Orysia Lutsevych believes Vladimir Putin has increased his calls for negotiations.
Orysia Lutsevych believes Vladimir Putin knows his window of opportunity may be closing.
Russia is considerably bigger and stronger than Ukraine.
Russia has not managed to fulfill its territorial goals in Ukraine.
Moscow’s initial attempt to take Kyiv ended in a defeat.
The front lines in Ukraine have not moved considerably in over a year.
New US military assistance began reaching the front lines in Ukraine in May.
Months of delays in US military assistance were caused by political deadlock in the US Congress.
Ukraine received permission from some Western nations to use their weapons to strike targets inside Russia.
This permission is limited to specific circumstances and areas near the Ukrainian border.
The new US military assistance and permission for strikes inside Russia have helped slow Russian progress.
These developments have averted a possible reoccupation of the Kharkiv region.
Ukraine is currently defending territory.
Ukraine is not currently pushing forward to reclaim areas under Russian occupation.
Riley Bailey is a Russia analyst at the US-based Institute for the Study of War.
Riley Bailey stated that Ukrainian forces will need to accumulate equipment, material, and manpower for a future counteroffensive operation.
Riley Bailey stated that the Russian military command appears to be pursuing a strategy of consistent, grinding offensive operations along the entire front line.
The front line in Ukraine is more than 600 miles (1,000 kilometers) long.
Russia is making gradual, creeping advances along the front line.
Riley Bailey stated that Russia's advances are forcing Ukraine to commit to defensive operations.
Riley Bailey stated that Russia's advances are preventing Ukraine from gearing up for a counteroffensive.
Riley Bailey stated that Ukrainian forces will need to degrade Russian forces and capabilities involved in offensive operations.
Riley Bailey stated that degrading Russian forces would provide Ukraine with more flexibility and ease pressure.
Riley Bailey stated that Ukraine could then make operational choices it has not been able to make recently.
The success of any future Ukrainian counteroffensive will primarily depend on the level of support from its Western allies.
Volodymyr Zelensky stated that the current level of support is sufficient to hold off further Russian advances.
Volodymyr Zelensky stated that the current level of support is not sufficient to win the war.
Donald Trump announced JD Vance as his vice-presidential nominee.
JD Vance has previously suggested Ukraine should negotiate with Russia because the US and other allies lack the capacity to support Ukraine.
Donald Trump has claimed he would "end the war in one day."
Donald Trump has stated that the US should not send money to Ukraine with no strings attached.
Germany plans to halve its military aid to Ukraine next year.
