John Herbst stated that serious people on Donald Trump's national security team would understand that Vladimir Putin is a direct threat to American interests.
John Herbst stated that serious people on Donald Trump's national security team would understand that it is important or critical for the US that Vladimir Putin loses in Ukraine.
John Herbst stated that another factor could convince a possible Trump administration to continue helping Ukraine.
John Herbst stated that if a Trump team cuts off aid and Ukraine collapses, it would be a major defeat for the United States caused by the Trump team.
John Herbst stated that such a defeat would overshadow the embarrassment and damage from Biden's withdrawal from Afghanistan.
John Herbst stated that people on a Trump team would understand this consequence.
Analysts expect the Ukraine aid package, which is more than $60 billion, to last Kyiv about a year to 18 months.
The US Congress approved this aid package earlier this year.
Analysts believe this timeframe could be enough for Ukraine to regroup and launch a new counteroffensive.
Orysia Lutsevych stated that Ukraine desperately needs to make battlefield gains.
Orysia Lutsevych stated that Russia's desire to negotiate does not currently appear genuine.
Orysia Lutsevych stated that Vladimir Putin is putting Russia on a total war footing.
Orysia Lutsevych stated that the war will likely end only if Moscow begins to feel threatened.
